Package: luma-launcher
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: sqlite3
Suggests: xdg-desktop-portal
Description: Native GTK4 application launcher
 Luma Launcher is a keyboard-driven application launcher for Linux desktops.
 It searches installed applications by name, description, keywords and
 acronyms, ranks them by your own launch history and desktop usage, and
 launches them through GIO without interpreting Exec fields itself.
 .
 It also provides a calculator, quick web searches, desktop actions, pinned
 favourites, dark, light and system themes, and a global shortcut through the
 desktop portal. Reading usage statistics on KDE needs the sqlite3 command.
